WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.933
In this Cloud Minute, I want to show you how to resize a persistent disk without downtime

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:07.933
Here, I have a Compute Engine VM called my-instance

00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:09.933
It has a disk attached called my-disk

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.566
Let's click on my-disk and take a look at its size

00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:13.833
It's 100 GB

00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:17.333
Let's go back to our instance and SSH into it

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.333
Look at the disk size using "df -h" command

00:00:26.333 --> 00:00:30.333
Now, let's go back to console and double our disk size

00:00:30.333 --> 00:00:33.333
Click on the disk

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:36.333
Click edit

00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:39.333
Change size to 200

00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:41.333
Hit Save

00:00:41.333 --> 00:00:44.333
After you resize your disk, you must resize your partition

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:46.833
so that operating system can access the additional space 

00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:49.833
Let's do that using "resize2fs" command

00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:54.333
Note that you didn't have to reboot or even start a new shell

00:00:54.333 --> 00:00:57.333
Now, let's see that it is resized

00:00:57.333 --> 00:00:59.900
That's it! Thanks for watching

